{"opencli":"0.1-draft","info":{"title":"onemedia","version":"0.8.0-preview.3","description":"The onemedia command line tool: inspect media containers, edit tags, remux, trim, make files playable, strip location and device identifiers, repair damaged files and rebuild cut-off recordings, and convert and extract subtitles. Remux also writes MPEG-TS/M2TS and WAV/BWF/RF64. `package` writes CMAF or transport-stream segments with HLS playlists and a DASH MPD (preview). Containers, metadata, subtitles; no decoding. Unaffiliated with other products or companies named OneMedia."},"x-inspectra":{"artifactSource":"crawled-from-help","generator":"InSpectra.Gen","helpDocumentCount":1},"commands":[{"name":"concat","hidden":false,"description":"join files whose tracks match, without re-encoding","arguments":[{"name":"OUT","required":true,"hidden":false,"arity":{"minimum":1,"maximum":1}},{"name":"IN","required":true,"hidden":false,"arity":{"minimum":1,"maximum":1}}]},{"name":"events","hidden":false,"description":"list timecode tracks, SCTE 35 splice messages, ID3 timed metadata and emsg events with their times (a transport stream is read through once; --limit caps the events shown per stream, default 200)","options":[{"name":"--json","recursive":false,"hidden":false},{"name":"--limit","recursive":false,"hidden":false,"arguments":[{"name":"N","required":true,"arity":{"minimum":1,"maximum":1}}]}],"arguments":[{"name":"FILE","required":true,"hidden":false,"arity":{"minimum":1,"maximum":1}}]},{"name":"info","hidden":false,"description":"format, duration, tracks, facts with every candidate, and defects (sidecars beside the file count as evidence; --telemetry also decodes GPS telemetry into the facts; --file-times adds the file's last-write time as a last-resort capture time)","options":[{"name":"--json","recursive":false,"hidden":false},{"name":"--no-sidecars","recursive":false,"hidden":false},{"name":"--telemetry","recursive":false,"hidden":false},{"name":"--file-times","recursive":fal